  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity building for the food and horticulture industry in Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project supports implementing a bi-annual action strategic plan (2021-2022) to provide technical assistance and strengthen the capacities of local key private stakeholders and government institutions of the horticulture sector in Colombia. The goal is to help raise the level of Colombian horticulture in terms of productivity, quality and sustainability through improving the current production practices and technologies. The project supports the local horticulture sector with specialized capacity building that will enable transforming the horticulture sector towards a more sustainable and competitive practice. That further enables local small farmers of the regions of Boyac&#xe1;, Cundinamarca, Antioquia, Magdalena and Cesar in Colombia to access the horticulture supply chain and to connect them with high-end actors of the national and international markets. The project also contributes to identifying opportunities for connecting the Dutch and the Colombian horticulture sectors. That may foster the development of the export potential of Colombia in vegetables.</narrative>
  </description>
